@oracle-en1998-1-compliance-independent
@comparison-numerical-v1
Feature: EN 1998 check outcome of committed documents
  A committed before-snapshot of the mutation fixtures is evaluated by the production report and by the independent seismic utilisations of `../../🔮️oracles/🚦️check-outcome/🐍️.py` (EN 1998-1 spectrum, lateral force method, storey shears, drift, P-delta, torsion, regularity, overturning, joint gap, non-structural force, capacity design and member detailing per building, the tie beams and slopes of EN 1998-5, the Annex E wall thrust and water thrust of every retaining wall and the 5.4.1.1 foundation sliding, system, storey and member).
  Each row names one check id, its status (pass at a utilisation of at most 1, fail above 1) and its utilisation; rows were picked away from the near-limit band so the status is unambiguous.

